notarization and closing, credit and real estate information, and search and valuation management services. It serves homebuyers and sellers, residential and commercial real estate professionals, mortgage lenders and servicers, title agencies and real estate attorneys, and home builders through direct operations, network of independent agencies, and other businesses. Stewart Information Services Corporation was founded in 1893 and is headquartered in Houston, Texas.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Frederick Henry Eppinger Jr. | CEO & Director | Age 66 | Compensation: $3.5M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 7K people. Revenue per employee of $375K ranks in the below the sector median among Financial Services peers. Each employee generates $17K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $2K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 9\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (3/10).","financial_summary":["Stewart Information Services Co is a small-cap financial services business with a $1.4B market cap on $2.9B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -2% over the past three years and +4% annually across the full decade \u2014 essentially flat, and a business treading water is rarely a path to compounding.","Returns on capital run at 10% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically.","The business throws off $132M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 5 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.78\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage runs at 10.3\u00d7.","Net dilution runs at 5.5% annually, transferring value from owners 